--- !u!114 &583279520
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 583279518}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0779e4ba6c0e4c74686c39804d9cc14c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Route24.GameOff.TutorialUIController
  _skipCanvas: {fileID: 1671630182}
  _skipText: {fileID: 36673404}
  _skipFillBar: {fileID: 1632926332}
  _checklistCanvas: {fileID: 1904915730}
  _detailsCanvas: {fileID: 677094512}
  _detailsText: {fileID: 1590410760}
  _steps:
  - checklistText: {fileID: 1231165099}
    checklistLabel: Start Inspection
    explanation: Welcome new recruit! Lets take you through a routine inspection
      to get you familiar with the process. First off, lets start an inspection by
      pressing [E] on the inspection button.
  - checklistText: {fileID: 299727163}
    checklistLabel: Focus Cargo Manifest
    explanation: Now, below the inspection button is the Cargo Manifest console.
      This console will provide you with a list of banned cargo for the day and allows
      you to see the cargo which the ship is carrying. Press [E] to focus on this
      console.
  - checklistText: {fileID: 1694716329}
    checklistLabel: Scan Scrambled Entry
    explanation: You can now use the up/down arrows to navigate the ship's cargo
      items, and if an entry is unclear, you can press [SPACE] to scan it. You are
      not required to scan every item, if you familiarise yourself with the daily
      banned list you can try guess if the ship is carrying banned cargo or not,
      scan the scrambled entry to continue.
  - checklistText: {fileID: 1599831628}
    checklistLabel: Power Main Console
    explanation: Find the power switch for main console and turn it on by pressing
      [E].
  - checklistText: {fileID: 1921486945}
    checklistLabel: Focus Oscillator
    explanation: You can now focus the Oscillator console by looking at it and pressing
      [E].
  - checklistText: {fileID: 1593907762}
    checklistLabel: Match Signal
    explanation: Every incoming ship will have a signal [GREEN] which you need to
      match with your signal [ORANGE]. In order to do this, you need to adjust the
      knobs below the screen using [LEFT CLICK] and dragging. Match up the signal
      to continue.
  - checklistText: {fileID: 723875059}
    checklistLabel: Power Keypad
    explanation: The final step is to enter the clearance code, find the keypad power
      switch and turn it on by pressing [E].
  - checklistText: {fileID: 1470808677}
    checklistLabel: Clearance Code
    explanation: You will find the clearance code on the Cargo Manifest console,
      then enter it on the keypad by looking at the buttons and pressing [LEFT CLICK].
      If you want a closer look at any part of the console, you can just press [RIGHT
      CLICK].
  - checklistText: {fileID: 1337332160}
    checklistLabel: Approve / Decline
    explanation: Now that you've completed the signal matching and clearance code,
      you can go ahead and approve or decline the ship. The responsibility lies on
      you to make the correct decision, any ships with banned cargo being approved
      will result in a penalty, and eventual termination.
  - checklistText: {fileID: 792780287}
    checklistLabel: Power Lights
    explanation: Find the power switch for the lights and press [E] to turn them
      on.
  - checklistText: {fileID: 551647187}
    checklistLabel: Open Dock
    explanation: Lets open up the dock for inspection by opening the docking gates.
